# `meta-bsp-jr`

**Yocto-Based BSP Layer for Embedded Systems**

A Yocto Project Board Support Package (BSP) layer providing **machine configurations** and hardware-specific settings for embedded Linux platforms.

---

## Overview

The **meta-bsp-jr** layer provides **machine definitions** and platform-specific configurations to extend Yocto builds.
It introduces board support packages (BSPs) for selected embedded devices, covering kernel, bootloader, and device-tree setups required to bring the hardware up.

---

## Adding the Layer to Your Build

```bash
bitbake-layers add-layer path/to/meta-bsp-jr
```

Then update your `bblayers.conf` with this layer and its dependencies.
Select a machine introduced by this BSP, for example:

```bash
MACHINE = "your-machine-name"
```

---

## Layer Structure

```text
meta-bsp-jr/
├── conf/                      # Layer and machine configuration
│   └── machine/               # Machine definitions
├── recipes-kernel/            # Kernel recipes, patches, and configs
├── recipes-bsp/               # Bootloader or low-level BSP recipes
├── COPYING.MIT                # License
└── README.md                  # This README
```

